# Keep the build context small and the image free of things it must not carry.
# Note this file governs what Docker can SEE, so anything COPY needs must be
# absent from here -- see the model/data notes below, which are the two
# non-obvious cases.

# --- Version control / CI ---
.git
.github
.gitignore

# --- Local Python environments and caches ---
venv/
.venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# --- Test + coverage output ---
htmlcov/
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml

# --- Not needed at runtime ---
tests/
notebooks/
scripts/
docs/
Report/
reports/
sdk/
*.md

# --- Local databases and dev state ---
*.db
*.db-journal
dump.rdb
.claude/
.DS_Store

# --- Node tooling for the extension's tests (no build step for MV3) ---
extension/node_modules/

# --- Training data: large, and never read at serving time ---
# The exceptions below are deliberate and load-bearing:
#   * data/reference/  -- brands.json IS read at boot by the detection layer
#   * data/raw/feeds/  -- the PhishTank snapshot IS read at boot by the
#                         threat-intel pre-filter
#   * data/processed/  -- train.parquet is the SHAP explainer's background
#                         sample; without it the app still boots but /explain
#                         is disabled (create_app logs a warning and skips it)
data/raw/*.csv
data/raw/*.arff

# NOT ignored, and intentionally so: models/production/*.joblib and
# metadata.json. They are git-ignored (Iron Law #5) but MUST be present in the
# build context, because create_app() refuses to start without them. Build
# from a checkout where `scripts/train.py` + `scripts/evaluate.py` have been
# run, or mount them at runtime instead.
models/latest/
